@startuml components_diagram
title plogic - Components diagram

component "UI" as UI
component "Orchestrator" as Orchestrator
component "Scanner" as Scanner
component "Parser" as Parser
component "Simplifier" as Simplifier
component "Interpreter" as Interpreter

note top of UI
  The only impure component: reads the command line,
  files and terminal, and presents one truth table
  per proposition with its classification.
end note

note bottom of Scanner
  Tokenizes the source. Newline is a real token:
  it terminates a proposition.
end note

note bottom of Parser
  Builds the syntax tree (AST): one expression per
  proposition (batch parse), synchronizing to the
  next line after a parse error.
end note

note bottom of Simplifier
  Optional: skipped with --no-simplificar. Erases
  grouping first, then applies the laws as oriented
  rewrites to a fixed point. Weight never increases and
  strictly decreases whenever a rewrite applies.
end note

note bottom of Interpreter
  Evaluates the expression it receives (the original by
  default, the simplified one with --tabla-simplificada)
  and builds the truth table. A table of more than 4096
  rows is refused before enumeration.
end note

UI -down-> Orchestrator : 1. source text
Orchestrator -up-> UI #2E7D32 : 10. truth tables

Orchestrator -down-> Scanner : 2. source
Scanner -up-> Orchestrator #2E7D32 : 3. tokens

Orchestrator -down-> Parser : 4. tokens
Parser -up-> Orchestrator #2E7D32 : 5. expressions

note bottom of Orchestrator
  Steps 6-9 repeat once per parsed proposition;
  steps 1-5 and 10 happen once per run.
  Step 8 chooses the original expression by default,
  or the simplified one with --tabla-simplificada.
  A failing stage returns Err on the same arrow and
  the run stops: no truth tables are produced.
end note

Orchestrator -down-> Simplifier : 6. expression
Simplifier -up-> Orchestrator #2E7D32 : 7. simplified expression

Orchestrator -down-> Interpreter : 8. expression to tabulate
Interpreter -up-> Orchestrator #2E7D32 : 9. truth table

Scanner -[hidden]right- Parser
Parser -[hidden]right- Simplifier
Simplifier -[hidden]right- Interpreter

@enduml
